      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand you’re in a lot of discomfort, but it’s very important to stick to safe, recommended dosages of medications. Taking 3000mg or 4000mg of Tylenol (Acetaminophen) in one go is not safe and can be very harmful, possibly leading to liver failure. For adults, the maximum daily dose is typically 4000mg. In the event of severe pain, most doctors recommend taking smaller amounts more frequently, but it's crucial to consult a healthcare professional. They may suggest a different medication or pain management strategy that won't put your health at risk before you can get to a dentist.\n\nIn the meantime, try using ice packs on the cheek to help numb the area and reduce swelling, or over-the-counter topical anesthetics like benzocaine, but always follow the instructions carefully and consider potential allergic reactions. Seek advice from a pharmacist or your doctor for any medication advice, and get to a dentist as soon as possible. Your safety is the most important thing.",
